     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00020",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A26][/A26]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A26": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_365_07\" id=\"tag_17_365_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00022",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A27][/A27]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A27": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_365_08\" id=\"tag_17_365_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00023",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "It is common to suspend execution of a thread for an interval in order to poll the status of a non-interrupting function. A\nlarge number of actual needs can be met with a simple extension to [A28][I29]sleep[/I29]()[/A28] that\nprovides finer resolution.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sleep.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00024",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "In the POSIX.1-1990 standard and SVR4, it is possible to implement such a routine, but the frequency of wakeup is limited by the\nresolution of the [A30][I31]alarm[/I31]()[/A30] and [A32][I33]sleep[/I33]()[/A32]\nfunctions. In 4.3 BSD, it is possible to write such a routine using no static storage and reserving no system facilities. Although\nit is possible to write a function with similar functionality to [A34][I35]sleep[/I35]()[/A34] using the\nremainder of the [I36]timer_*[/I36]() functions, such a function requires the use of signals and the reservation of some signal number.\nThis volume of POSIX.1-2024 requires that [I37]nanosleep[/I37]() be non-intrusive of the signals function.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/alarm.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A32": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sleep.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A34": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sleep.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00025",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I38]nanosleep[/I38]() function shall return a value of 0 on success and -1 on failure or if interrupted. This latter case is\ndifferent from [A39][I40]sleep[/I40]()[/A39]. This was done because the remaining time is returned via an\nargument structure pointer, [I41]rmtp[/I41], instead of as the return value.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A39": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sleep.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I41": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
